The following standard commands are available.
For more information on a specific command, type:
   HELP  command name

ALIAS .... displays/sets aliases
ASSIGN ... logical to physical drive assignment
ATDIR .... changes the attributes of directories
ATTRIB ... changes the attributes of files
BASIC .... goes into MSX disk BASIC
BEEP ..... makes beeping sound
BOOT ..... assigns a new Nextor boot drive
BUFFERS .. displays/sets the number of disk buffers
CD ....... see CHDIR
CDD ...... displays/sets the current directory and drive
CDPATH ... displays/sets the directory search path
CHDIR .... displays/sets the current directory
CHKDSK ... checks the integrity of a disk
CLS ...... clears the screen
COLOR .... changes screen colors
CONCAT ... joins files together
COPY ..... copies files
CPU ...... displays/sets the CPU mode
DATE ..... displays/sets the current date
DEL ...... see ERASE
DEVINFO .. displays the devices handled by a disk driver
DIR ...... displays the file names on a disk
DIRB ..... same as DIR, with the sizes always in bytes
DISKCOPY . copies a whole disk to another
DRIVERS .. displays the disk drivers present in the system
DRVINFO .. displays what every drive is assigned to
DSKCHK ... displays/sets the current disk check status
ECHO ..... prints the following text
ECHOS .... prints the following text without a trailing CR/LF
ELSE ..... toggles Command Mode
END ...... ends batch file execution [.BTM]
ENDIFF ... restores Command Mode
ERA ...... see ERASE
ERASE .... deletes files
EXIT ..... exits COMMAND3.COM
FIXDISK .. updates MSX-DOS 1 disks to MSX-DOS 2
FORMAT ... formats a disk
FREE ..... displays total, used and free disk space
GOSUB .... calls a batch file sub-routine [.BTM]
GOTO ..... continues batch file from label [.BTM]
HELP ..... gives help information on a command
HERTZ .... sets the VDP VBlank refresh speed
HISTORY .. displays the command history list or resizes the history buffer
IF ....... executes command if equation is true
IFF ...... sets Command Mode ON if equation is true
INKEY .... reads character into environment item
INPUT .... reads string into environment item
KMODE .... sets or resets "Kanji Mode"
LOCK ..... locks/unlocks a drive
MAPDRV ... maps a drive to a device and partition or mounts a file
MD ....... see MKDIR
MEM ...... displays a compact memory mapper listing
MEMORY ... displays the amount and status of system RAM
MKDIR .... creates a new sub-directory
MODE ..... changes the screen mode
MOVE ..... moves files on a disk
MVDIR .... moves sub-directories
PATH ..... displays/sets the command search path
PAUSE .... prompts for a keypress
POPD ..... restores the current drive and directory
PUSHD .... stores the current drive and directory
RALLOC ... displays/sets the reduced allocation information mode
RAMDISK .. displays/sets the size of the RAM disk
RD ....... see RMDIR
REM ...... remark... Ignores the following text.
REN ...... see RENAME
RENAME ... renames files
RESET .... resets system
RETURN ... returns from a batch file sub-routine [.BTM]
RMDIR .... removes empty sub-directories
RNDIR .... renames sub-directories
SET ...... displays/sets environment strings
SHELLRAM . displays/sets the use of a RAM segment for shell features
SHIFT .... shifts arguments for a batch file one step to the left
THEN ..... executes the following command
TIME ..... displays/sets the current time
TO ....... changes to another directory
TREE ..... displays directories in a tree format
TYPE ..... displays the contents of files
UNDEL .... recovers deleted files
VER ...... displays Nextor version numbers
VERIFY ... displays/sets the current verify state
VOL ...... displays/sets disk volume name
XCOPY .... copies files from a directory tree
XDIR ..... displays filenames in a directory tree
Z80MODE .. displays/sets the Z80 access mode for a legacy driver

Help for other Nextor features is also available.
The standard topics are:

ALI ...... aliases and executable extensions
BATCH .... batch files
EDITING .. command line editing and re-entering
ENV ...... environment strings
ERRORS ... error messages and Abort, Retry errors
IO ....... redirection, piping and standard I/O
SYNTAX ... notation used in command descriptions
